From 1126a1c6d86a592bf2acfb6ddc466360ba7dcced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Kush)" <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:27:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] linux: compile out USD and DLSS-NR, GCC conformance
 fixes, NVAPI SAL shims

- REMIX_NO_USD guards for material/light USD deserialization, a no-op
  GameCapturer, and pxr includes in the PCH and matrix helpers.
- REMIX_NO_DLSSNR guards: DLSS-NR headers ship only in the Windows NGX
  package, so the feature reports unsupported.
- Standard C++ fixes that MSVC tolerated: dependent SFINAE defaults in
  RtxOption, deduced return types used before definition, non-trivial
  members in anonymous structs, brace assignment ambiguity.
- nvapi.h wrapper scopes Microsoft SAL macros to the include.

All RTX shaders compile and validate with slang v2025.10.4 plus the
cherry-picks in the port repo. dxvk_device.cpp passes a syntax check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb41TgDi74v7sgH5LJBZ5A
Signed-off-by: Claude (for Kush) <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
